<!-- ============================================================
     GoSerpent: Go-Based RAT - Southeast Asia Government Espionage
     MITRE ATT&amp;CK Techniques:
       T1573.001 - Encrypted Channel: Symmetric Cryptography (ChaCha20, SHA256-keyed)
       T1560     - Archive Collected Data (ThumbcacheService - thumbcache_605a.db)
       T1003.001 - OS Credential Dumping: LSASS Memory (Mimikatz + QuarksDumpLocalHash)
       T1090     - Proxy (Stowaway SOCKS5 port-forward / reverse tunnel C2 chain)
       T1036     - Masquerading (ThumbcacheService DLL masquerades as Windows component)
       T1574     - Hijack Execution Flow (TmcLoader stages payloads via DLL loading)
       T1003     - OS Credential Dumping (QuarksDumpLocalHash targets local account hashes)
     Rule IDs: 104112-104120
     Author: SecOps Engineer
     Date: 2026-07-21
     References:
       - Kaspersky Securelist (2026-07-17): securelist.com/goserpent-backdoor-in-southeast-asia/120687/
       - threat-intel/2026-07-17_securelist-goserpent-backdoor-southeast-asia-espionage.md
       - detections/collection/goserpent_thumbcacheservice_file_collection.md
     Attribution: Unattributed; China-nexus indicators (Alibaba Cloud / UCLOUD HK C2,
                  Stowaway SOCKS5 widely used by China-nexus groups, SEA gov targeting)
     Log source prerequisites:
       - Sysmon EventID 1  (ProcessCreate)  - Wazuh SID 61603
         Required for rules 104113-104119
       - Sysmon EventID 11 (FileCreate)     - Wazuh SID 61644
         Required for rule 104112 (thumbcache_605a.db artifact)
       - Sysmon EventID 10 (ProcessAccess)  - Wazuh SID 61603 with eventID filter
         Required for rule 104117 (LSASS handle open by Go RAT process)
       - Firewall/network logs (firewall group) with data.dest_ip
         Required for rule 104118 (Alibaba Cloud / UCLOUD HK egress)
     Coverage notes:
       - thumbcache_605a.db at C:\Users\Public\ is a HIGHLY SPECIFIC GoSerpent IOC;
         any host with this file should be treated as compromised immediately
       - C2 IPs are hosted exclusively on Alibaba Cloud and UCLOUD HK (11 IPs total;
         specific values not publicly released by Kaspersky); alert on those IP ranges
         from Windows servers with no business relationship to Chinese cloud providers
       - Stowaway, McMx, and TmcLoader are standalone Go binaries; they do not appear
         in standard Windows software inventories; any execution should be investigated
       - GoSerpent uses AES-CBC to decrypt its embedded configuration (C2 address +
         ChaCha20 session password) at runtime; binary analysis required for C2 extraction
     Severity tiers:
       15 - thumbcache_605a.db file creation (confirmed GoSerpent IOC; immediate response)
       14 - ThumbcacheService spawning credential dump or proxy tool (confirmed kill chain)
       13 - QuarksDumpLocalHash or Mimikatz/LSASS access (credential dumping stage)
       13 - Stowaway SOCKS5 proxy execution (C2 chaining tool)
       12 - TmcLoader or McMx execution (GoSerpent staging components)
       12 - ThumbcacheService execution from non-standard path (masquerading indicator)
       11 - Outbound from Windows host to Alibaba/UCLOUD HK ranges (possible GoSerpent C2)
     ============================================================ -->

<group name="threat_intel,espionage,goserpent,go_rat,sea_targeting,china_nexus,">

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Sysmon EventID 11 (FileCreate): ThumbcacheService artifact
       Rule ID: 104112
       C:\Users\Public\thumbcache_605a.db is the output file of the
       GoSerpent-deployed ThumbcacheService DLL. This path is unique:
       it masquerades as a Windows thumbnail cache database (thumbcache_*.db)
       but the 605a suffix and Public location do not correspond to any
       legitimate Windows thumbnail cache file. Any creation of a file
       matching this pattern at C:\Users\Public\ by any process is a
       confirmed GoSerpent ThumbcacheService indicator.
       Severity 15 (critical): treat this as a confirmed compromise IOC.
       =========================================================== -->

  <!-- ThumbcacheService drops GoSerpent collection archive (confirmed IOC) -->
  <rule id="104112" level="15">
    <if_sid>61644</if_sid>
    <field name="win.system.eventID">^11$</field>
    <field name="win.eventdata.targetFilename" type="pcre2">(?i)C:\\Users\\Public\\thumbcache_605a\.db$</field>
    <description>CRITICAL: GoSerpent ThumbcacheService IOC  -  file C:\Users\Public\thumbcache_605a.db created by $(win.eventdata.image) on $(win.eventdata.computer). Password-protected archive of harvested files; confirmed GoSerpent collection artifact. Treat as active compromise; initiate IR immediately. (T1560, T1036)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1560</id>
      <id>T1036</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>goserpent,thumbcacheservice,collection,confirmed_ioc,isolate_host,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Sysmon EventID 1 (ProcessCreate): GoSerpent toolset execution
       Rule IDs: 104113-104116
       The GoSerpent actor deploys a multi-component framework:
         - QuarksDumpLocalHash: dumps local account NTLM hashes;
           a less common credential dumper that generates a process
           named QuarksDumpLocalHash.exe or ql.exe
         - Stowaway: open-source Go SOCKS5 proxy / reverse tunnel;
           used to chain C2 through compromised hosts; binaries may
           be named stowaway.exe, stowaway, or custom variants
         - TmcLoader: Go loader that stages and executes other payloads;
           typically named tmcloader.exe or similar
         - McMx: simpler Go implant (proxy or secondary RAT); may appear
           as mcmx.exe or with legitimate-looking service names
       All are standalone Go binaries with large binary sizes (~3-10 MB)
       and CGO-linked characteristics; none are standard Windows software.
       =========================================================== -->

  <!-- QuarksDumpLocalHash credential dumper execution -->
  <rule id="104113" level="13">
    <if_sid>61603</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.image" type="pcre2">(?i)\\(QuarksDumpLocalHash|quarksdump|ql)\.exe$</field>
    <description>GoSerpent: QuarksDumpLocalHash credential dumper executed as $(win.eventdata.image) on $(win.eventdata.computer)  -  GoSerpent actor deploys this tool to harvest local NTLM account hashes. Investigate process tree and parent process $(win.eventdata.parentImage). (T1003)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1003</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>goserpent,credential_dumping,quarks_dump,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- Stowaway SOCKS5 proxy / reverse tunnel execution -->
  <rule id="104114" level="13">
    <if_sid>61603</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.image" type="pcre2">(?i)\\stowaway(\.exe)?$</field>
    <description>GoSerpent: Stowaway SOCKS5 reverse tunnel proxy executed as $(win.eventdata.image) on $(win.eventdata.computer)  -  GoSerpent actor chains C2 through compromised hosts using Stowaway to obscure traffic routing; widely used by China-nexus APT groups. Isolate host and trace upstream C2 chain. (T1090, T1573.001)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1090</id>
      <id>T1573.001</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>goserpent,stowaway,c2_proxy,china_nexus,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- TmcLoader payload staging component -->
  <rule id="104115" level="12">
    <if_sid>61603</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.image" type="pcre2">(?i)\\(tmcloader|tmc_loader|TmcLoader)(\.exe)?$</field>
    <description>GoSerpent: TmcLoader staging component executed as $(win.eventdata.image) on $(win.eventdata.computer)  -  Go-based loader that stages and executes GoSerpent, McMx, ThumbcacheService, and Stowaway payloads. Active GoSerpent intrusion underway; investigate immediately. (T1574)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1574</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>goserpent,tmcloader,loader,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- McMx secondary Go implant execution -->
  <rule id="104116" level="12">
    <if_sid>61603</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.image" type="pcre2">(?i)\\(mcmx|McMx)(\.exe)?$</field>
    <description>GoSerpent: McMx secondary Go implant executed as $(win.eventdata.image) on $(win.eventdata.computer)  -  simpler Go proxy or secondary RAT deployed alongside GoSerpent primary RAT; used for C2 failover or lateral movement relay. Investigate full process tree. (T1090, T1573.001)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1090</id>
      <id>T1573.001</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>goserpent,mcmx,secondary_rat,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Sysmon EventID 10 (ProcessAccess): LSASS handle open
       Rule ID: 104117
       GoSerpent actor deploys Mimikatz for plaintext credential
       harvesting and NTLM hash theft via LSASS memory reads.
       This rule detects any process opening a read handle to lsass.exe
       and is wider than just GoSerpent; it catches the Mimikatz and
       QuarksDumpLocalHash pattern without requiring a specific process name,
       making it resilient to binary renaming.
       Uses the Sysmon EventID 10 filter via the 61603 parent SID with
       win.system.eventID check (pattern established in purple_team_phase1.xml).
       =========================================================== -->

  <!-- LSASS handle open (Mimikatz / QuarksDumpLocalHash pattern) -->
  <rule id="104117" level="13">
    <if_sid>61603</if_sid>
    <field name="win.system.eventID">^10$</field>
    <field name="win.eventdata.targetImage" type="pcre2">(?i)\\lsass\.exe$</field>
    <field name="win.eventdata.sourceImage" negate="yes" type="pcre2">(?i)\\(MsMpEng|svchost|csrss|wininit|services|lsass|winlogon|NisSrv|MsSense|SenseCnfg|SecurityHealthService|AggregatorHost|spoolsv|dwm|System)\.exe$</field>
    <description>GoSerpent/Mimikatz: $(win.eventdata.sourceImage) opened handle to lsass.exe on $(win.eventdata.computer)  -  credential harvesting attempt; GoSerpent actor uses Mimikatz and QuarksDumpLocalHash for NTLM hash and plaintext credential theft. Investigate source process immediately. (T1003.001)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1003.001</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>goserpent,mimikatz,credential_dumping,lsass,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Firewall: Outbound from Windows hosts to Chinese cloud providers
       Rule ID: 104118
       GoSerpent C2 nodes are hosted exclusively on Alibaba Cloud and
       UCLOUD HK. For homelab/enterprise environments with no business
       relationship to Chinese cloud providers, outbound connections
       from Windows servers (especially east-west or server-to-external)
       to Alibaba Cloud (AS37963, 47.0.0.0/8, 8.210.0.0/16, etc.)
       or UCLOUD HK (AS135377, 103.74.0.0/15) warrant investigation.
       This rule triggers on Alibaba Cloud's primary CIDR blocks;
       expand to full AS37963/AS135377 prefix list if available.
       NOTE: Also triggered by Stowaway SOCKS5 relay hops; internal
       east-west connections from non-C2-hosts to these ranges after
       initial compromise may indicate Stowaway lateral relay.
       =========================================================== -->

  <!-- Outbound to Alibaba Cloud / UCLOUD HK ranges (GoSerpent C2 hosting) -->
  <rule id="104118" level="11">
    <if_group>firewall</if_group>
    <field name="data.dest_ip" type="pcre2">^(47\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+|8\.210\.\d+\.\d+|8\.211\.\d+\.\d+|8\.212\.\d+\.\d+|8\.213\.\d+\.\d+|47\.74\.\d+\.\d+|103\.74\.\d+\.\d+|103\.75\.\d+\.\d+)$</field>
    <description>GoSerpent C2 candidate: outbound from $(data.src_ip) to Alibaba Cloud / UCLOUD HK IP $(data.dest_ip)  -  GoSerpent actor hosts all C2 nodes exclusively on Alibaba Cloud and UCLOUD HK; Chinese-provider egress from Windows hosts with no business relationship warrants investigation. Cross-reference with Stowaway execution events. (T1573.001, T1090)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1573.001</id>
      <id>T1090</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>goserpent,c2_egress,alibaba_cloud,ucloud,china_nexus,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       Composite indicator: ThumbcacheService process spawning known
       credential dumping or proxy tool (high-confidence kill chain)
       Rule ID: 104119
       If ThumbcacheService (the GoSerpent collection DLL host process)
       spawns QuarksDumpLocalHash or Stowaway, the intrusion is confirmed
       with very high confidence across two distinct TTPs (T1560 + T1003
       or T1560 + T1090). This two-event chain is too specific to be
       coincidental.
       =========================================================== -->

  <!-- ThumbcacheService process spawning credential dump or SOCKS5 proxy tool -->
  <rule id="104119" level="14">
    <if_sid>61603</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.parentImage" type="pcre2">(?i)\\(ThumbcacheService|thumbcache)(\.exe|\.dll)?$</field>
    <field name="win.eventdata.image" type="pcre2">(?i)\\(QuarksDumpLocalHash|quarksdump|ql|stowaway|tmcloader|tmc_loader|mcmx|McMx)(\.exe)?$</field>
    <description>CRITICAL: GoSerpent multi-stage toolchain confirmed  -  ThumbcacheService ($(win.eventdata.parentImage)) spawned $(win.eventdata.image) on $(win.eventdata.computer). Two-TTP chain (collection + credential dump/proxy) is definitive GoSerpent IOC. Initiate IR immediately. (T1560, T1003/T1090)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1560</id>
      <id>T1003</id>
      <id>T1090</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>goserpent,confirmed_ioc,multi_stage,isolate_host,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       ThumbcacheService DLL-host process anomaly (broad detection)
       Rule ID: 104120
       ThumbcacheService is not a standard Windows service or component
       name. Any process executing under this name from a non-Windows
       system directory is inherently suspicious. This broad rule fires
       for any ThumbcacheService execution that has not already matched
       the more specific rule 104112 (file drop) or 104119 (child spawn).
       =========================================================== -->

  <!-- ThumbcacheService process created outside Windows system directories -->
  <rule id="104120" level="12">
    <if_sid>61603</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.image" type="pcre2">(?i)\\ThumbcacheService(\.exe|\.dll)?$</field>
    <field name="win.eventdata.image" negate="yes" type="pcre2">(?i)^C:\\Windows\\(System32|SysWOW64|WinSxS)\\</field>
    <description>GoSerpent: ThumbcacheService process $(win.eventdata.image) executed from non-standard path on $(win.eventdata.computer)  -  GoSerpent deploys a malicious DLL masquerading as a Windows thumbnail cache service; legitimate Windows has no ThumbcacheService component outside System32. Investigate parent $(win.eventdata.parentImage) and loaded DLLs. (T1036, T1574)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1036</id>
      <id>T1574</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>goserpent,thumbcacheservice,masquerading,</group>
  </rule>

</group>
